## And one thing I'd change from my previous recommendation

I **wouldn't create a giant `UI/` at the root** and move all UI into it.

For Rihla, UI belongs with the feature it serves.

So:

```text
Inventory/UI/
Player/UI/
Interaction/UI/
```

is better than:

```text
UI/
├── Inventory/
├── Player/
└── Interaction/
```

because when you're working on Inventory, **everything related to Inventory is in one place**.

That's particularly important for the system you've built: `BPC_Inventory`, `DT_ItemData`, `S_ItemSlot`, `WBP_ItemTool`, `WBP_InventoryUI`, `WBP_QuickSelectMenu`, etc. are all parts of one gameplay feature even though they are technically different asset types.

**That's the architecture I'd stick with for Rihla going forward.**
